{
  "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1112.2967",
  "prompt": "Find quantitative statements about: Ulysses fast and slow solar wind bulk properties (Ebert et al. 2009, McComas et al. 2000) — speed, density scaled to 1 AU, temperature, B; the density-speed anticorrelation and invariance of dynamic pressure or energy flux with latitude/speed (e.g., McComas 2008, Le Chat 2012, Phillips 1995); any formula relating density to speed used for modeling. Quote verbatim with section/equation/table numbers."
}

{
  "command": "S=/tmp/claude-1000/-mnt-c-Users-cabot-OneDrive-Documents-Research-Cambridge-X3I/c4794a53-4881-4aa9-8b9b-7c033457fa8b/scratchpad; T=/home/scabot/.claude/projects/-mnt-c-Users-cabot-OneDrive-Documents-Research-Cambridge-X3I/c4794a53-4881-4aa9-8b9b-7c033457fa8b/tool-results; cp $T/webfetch-1792192771052-qxjyj2.pdf $S/pdfs/bzowski2013.pdf; cd $S && python3 -I scripts/ex.py pdfs/bzowski2013.pdf txt/bzowski2013.txt; head -c 300 txt/bzowski2013.txt; grep -n -a -i -E \"Ebert|McComas et al. \\(2000|Le Chat|dynamic pressure|energy flux|invarian\" txt/bzowski2013.txt | head -40",
